1.1.18.2 The `future_builtins' module
.....................................

Python 3.0 makes many changes to the repertoire of built-in functions,
and most of the changes can't be introduced in the Python 2.x series
because they would break compatibility.  The *note future_builtins: 6.
module provides versions of these built-in functions that can be
imported when writing 3.0-compatible code.

  The functions in this module currently include:

   * `ascii(obj)': equivalent to *note repr: f6.  In Python 3.0, *note
     repr: f6. will return a Unicode string, while `ascii()' will
     return a pure ASCII bytestring.

   * `filter(predicate, iterable)', `map(func, iterable1, ...)': the
     3.0 versions return iterators, unlike the 2.x builtins which
     return lists.

   * `hex(value)', `oct(value)': instead of calling the *note __hex__:
     f7. or *note __oct__: f8. methods, these versions will call the
     *note __index__: f9. method and convert the result to hexadecimal
     or octal.  *note oct: 6d. will use the new `0o' notation for its
     result.


