4.3.4.9 Emulating callable objects
..................................

 -- Method: object.__call__ (self[, args...])
     Called when the instance is "called" as a function; if this method
     is defined, `x(arg1, arg2, ...)' is a shorthand for
     `x.__call__(arg1, arg2, ...)'.


