5.5.6.3 XRange Type
...................

The *note xrange: 259. type is an immutable sequence which is commonly
used for looping.  The advantage of the *note xrange: 259. type is that
an *note xrange: 259.  object will always take the same amount of
memory, no matter the size of the range it represents.  There are no
consistent performance advantages.

  XRange objects have very little behavior: they only support indexing,
iteration, and the *note len: 33a. function.


