5.8.1 `datetime' -- Basic date and time types
---------------------------------------------

New in version 2.3.

  The *note datetime: ac. module supplies classes for manipulating
dates and times in both simple and complex ways.  While date and time
arithmetic is supported, the focus of the implementation is on
efficient member extraction for output formatting and manipulation. For
related functionality, see also the *note time: f0. and *note calendar:
305. modules.

  There are two kinds of date and time objects: "naive" and "aware".
This distinction refers to whether the object has any notion of time
zone, daylight saving time, or other kind of algorithmic or political
time adjustment.  Whether a naive *note datetime: ac. object represents
Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), local time, or time in some other
timezone is purely up to the program, just like it's up to the program
whether a particular number represents metres, miles, or mass.  Naive
*note datetime: ac. objects are easy to understand and to work with, at
the cost of ignoring some aspects of reality.

  For applications requiring more, *note datetime: ac. and *note time:
f0. objects have an optional time zone information member, *note
tzinfo: 84d, that can contain an instance of a subclass of the abstract
*note tzinfo: 84d. class.  These *note tzinfo: 84d. objects capture
information about the offset from UTC time, the time zone name, and
whether Daylight Saving Time is in effect.  Note that no concrete *note
tzinfo: 84d. classes are supplied by the *note datetime: ac. module.
Supporting timezones at whatever level of detail is required is up to
the application.  The rules for time adjustment across the world are
more political than rational, and there is no standard suitable for
every application.

  The *note datetime: ac. module exports the following constants:

 -- Data: datetime.MINYEAR
     The smallest year number allowed in a *note date: ee. or *note
     datetime: ac. object.  *note MINYEAR: 84e. is `1'.

 -- Data: datetime.MAXYEAR
     The largest year number allowed in a *note date: ee. or *note
     datetime: ac. object.  *note MAXYEAR: 84f. is `9999'.

Module *note calendar: 305.
     General calendar related functions.

Module *note time: f0.
     Time access and conversions.

* Menu:

* Available Types::
* timedelta Objects::
* date Objects::
* datetime Objects::
* time Objects::
* tzinfo Objects::
* strftime and strptime Behavior::


