5.8.1.1 Available Types
.......................

 -- Class: datetime.date
     An idealized naive date, assuming the current Gregorian calendar
     always was, and always will be, in effect. Attributes: `year',
     `month', and `day'.

 -- Class: datetime.time
     An idealized time, independent of any particular day, assuming
     that every day has exactly 24*60*60 seconds (there is no notion of
     "leap seconds" here).  Attributes: `hour', `minute', `second',
     `microsecond', and *note tzinfo: 84d.

 -- Class: datetime.datetime
     A combination of a date and a time. Attributes: `year', `month',
     `day', `hour', `minute', `second', `microsecond', and *note
     tzinfo: 84d.

 -- Class: datetime.timedelta
     A duration expressing the difference between two *note date: ee,
     *note time: f0, or *note datetime: ac. instances to microsecond
     resolution.

 -- Class: datetime.tzinfo
     An abstract base class for time zone information objects.  These
     are used by the *note datetime: ac. and *note time: f0. classes to
     provide a customizable notion of time adjustment (for example, to
     account for time zone and/or daylight saving time).

  Objects of these types are immutable.

  Objects of the *note date: ee. type are always naive.

  An object _d_ of type *note time: f0. or *note datetime: ac. may be
naive or aware.  _d_ is aware if `d.tzinfo' is not `None' and
`d.tzinfo.utcoffset(d)' does not return `None'.  If `d.tzinfo' is
`None', or if `d.tzinfo' is not `None' but `d.tzinfo.utcoffset(d)'
returns `None', _d_ is naive.

  The distinction between naive and aware doesn't apply to *note
timedelta: 851.  objects.

  Subclass relationships:

    object
        timedelta
        tzinfo
        time
        date
            datetime



