5.8.3 `collections' -- High-performance container datatypes
-----------------------------------------------------------

New in version 2.4.

  This module implements high-performance container datatypes.
Currently, there are two datatypes, *note deque: 151. and *note
defaultdict: 69e, and one datatype factory function, *note namedtuple:
8da.

  Changed in version 2.5: Added *note defaultdict: 69e.

  Changed in version 2.6: Added *note namedtuple: 8da.

  The specialized containers provided in this module provide
alternatives to Python's general purpose built-in containers, *note
dict: 39, *note list: 198, *note set: 11b, and *note tuple: 1f5.

  Besides the containers provided here, the optional *note bsddb: a4.
module offers the ability to create in-memory or file based ordered
dictionaries with string keys using the *note bsddb btopen: 8db. method.

  In addition to containers, the collections module provides some ABCs
(abstract base classes) that can be used to test whether a class
provides a particular interface, for example, is it hashable or a
mapping.

  Changed in version 2.6: Added abstract base classes.

* Menu:

* ABCs - abstract base classes::
* deque objects::
* defaultdict objects::
* namedtuple Factory Function for Tuples with Named Fields::


