5.8.3.4 `defaultdict' objects
.............................

 -- Class: collections.defaultdict ([default_factory[, ...]])
     Returns a new dictionary-like object.  *note defaultdict: 69e. is
     a subclass of the built-in *note dict: 39. class.  It overrides
     one method and adds one writable instance variable.  The remaining
     functionality is the same as for the *note dict: 39. class and is
     not documented here.

     The first argument provides the initial value for the *note
     default_factory: 8ea.  attribute; it defaults to `None'. All
     remaining arguments are treated the same as if they were passed to
     the *note dict: 39. constructor, including keyword arguments.

     New in version 2.5.

     *note defaultdict: 69e. objects support the following method in
     addition to the standard *note dict: 39. operations:

      -- Method: __missing__ (key)
          If the *note default_factory: 8ea. attribute is `None', this
          raises a *note KeyError: 1e1. exception with the _key_ as
          argument.

          If *note default_factory: 8ea. is not `None', it is called
          without arguments to provide a default value for the given
          _key_, this value is inserted in the dictionary for the
          _key_, and returned.

          If calling *note default_factory: 8ea. raises an exception
          this exception is propagated unchanged.

          This method is called by the *note __getitem__: 24b. method
          of the *note dict: 39. class when the requested key is not
          found; whatever it returns or raises is then returned or
          raised by *note __getitem__: 24b.

     *note defaultdict: 69e. objects support the following instance
     variable:

      -- Attribute: default_factory
          This attribute is used by the *note __missing__: 8eb. method;
          it is initialized from the first argument to the constructor,
          if present, or to `None', if absent.

