5.8.19.2 Subclassing Repr Objects
.................................

The use of dynamic dispatching by *note Repr repr1: 9c7. allows
subclasses of *note Repr: 9b8. to add support for additional built-in
object types or to modify the handling of types already supported. This
example shows how special support for file objects could be added:

    import repr as reprlib
    import sys

    class MyRepr(reprlib.Repr):
        def repr_file(self, obj, level):
            if obj.name in ['<stdin>', '<stdout>', '<stderr>']:
                return obj.name
            else:
                return repr(obj)

    aRepr = MyRepr()
    print aRepr.repr(sys.stdin)          # prints '<stdin>'



