5.9.1.1 The numeric tower
.........................

 -- Class: numbers.Complex
     Subclasses of this type describe complex numbers and include the
     operations that work on the built-in *note complex: 88. type.
     These are: conversions to *note complex: 88. and *note bool: 236,
     *note real: 9d0, *note imag: 9d1, `+', `-', `*', `/', *note abs:
     3c9, *note conjugate: 9d2, `==', and `!='. All except `-' and `!='
     are abstract.

      -- Attribute: real
          Abstract. Retrieves the real component of this number.

      -- Attribute: imag
          Abstract. Retrieves the imaginary component of this number.

      -- Method: conjugate ()
          Abstract. Returns the complex conjugate. For example,
          `(1+3j).conjugate() == (1-3j)'.

 -- Class: numbers.Real
     To *note Complex: 4f6, *note Real: 4f5. adds the operations that
     work on real numbers.

     In short, those are: a conversion to *note float: 85, `trunc()',
     *note round: 79, *note math floor: 7a, *note math ceil: 7b, *note
     divmod: 57a, `//', `%', `<', `<=', `>', and `>='.

     Real also provides defaults for *note complex: 88, *note real: 9d0,
     *note imag: 9d1, and *note conjugate: 9d2.

 -- Class: numbers.Rational
     Subtypes *note Real: 4f5. and adds *note numerator: 9d3. and *note
     denominator: 9d4. properties, which should be in lowest terms.
     With these, it provides a default for *note float: 85.

      -- Attribute: numerator
          Abstract.

      -- Attribute: denominator
          Abstract.

 -- Class: numbers.Integral
     Subtypes *note Rational: 78. and adds a conversion to *note int:
     6e.  Provides defaults for *note float: 85, *note numerator: 9d3,
     and *note denominator: 9d4, and bit-string operations: `<<', `>>',
     `&', `^', `|', `~'.


