5.9.8.1 `partial' Objects
.........................

*note partial: ae6. objects are callable objects created by *note
partial: ae6. They have three read-only attributes:

 -- Attribute: partial.func
     A callable object or function.  Calls to the *note partial: ae6.
     object will be forwarded to *note func: aea. with new arguments
     and keywords.

 -- Attribute: partial.args
     The leftmost positional arguments that will be prepended to the
     positional arguments provided to a *note partial: ae6. object call.

 -- Attribute: partial.keywords
     The keyword arguments that will be supplied when the *note
     partial: ae6. object is called.

  *note partial: ae6. objects are like `function' objects in that they
are callable, weak referencable, and can have attributes.  There are
some important differences.  For instance, the `__name__' and `__doc__'
attributes are not created automatically.  Also, *note partial: ae6.
objects defined in classes behave like static methods and do not
transform into bound methods during instance attribute look-up.


