5.12.5.2 TarInfo Objects
........................

A *note TarInfo: d46. object represents one member in a *note TarFile:
d2e. Aside from storing all required attributes of a file (like file
type, size, time, permissions, owner etc.), it provides some useful
methods to determine its type.  It does _not_ contain the file's data
itself.

  *note TarInfo: d46. objects are returned by *note TarFile: d2e.'s
methods `getmember()', `getmembers()' and `gettarinfo()'.

 -- Class: tarfile.TarInfo (name="")
     Create a *note TarInfo: d46. object.

 -- Method: TarInfo.frombuf (buf)
     Create and return a *note TarInfo: d46. object from string buffer
     _buf_.

     New in version 2.6: Raises *note HeaderError: d3b. if the buffer
     is invalid..

 -- Method: TarInfo.fromtarfile (tarfile)
     Read the next member from the *note TarFile: d2e. object _tarfile_
     and return it as a *note TarInfo: d46. object.

     New in version 2.6.

 -- Method: TarInfo.tobuf (format=DEFAULT_FORMAT, encoding=ENCODING,
          errors='strict')
     Create a string buffer from a *note TarInfo: d46. object. For
     information on the arguments see the constructor of the *note
     TarFile: d2e. class.

     Changed in version 2.6: The arguments were added.

  A `TarInfo' object has the following public data attributes:

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.name
     Name of the archive member.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.size
     Size in bytes.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.mtime
     Time of last modification.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.mode
     Permission bits.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.type
     File type.  _type_ is usually one of these constants: `REGTYPE',
     `AREGTYPE', `LNKTYPE', `SYMTYPE', `DIRTYPE', `FIFOTYPE',
     `CONTTYPE', `CHRTYPE', `BLKTYPE', `GNUTYPE_SPARSE'.  To determine
     the type of a *note TarInfo: d46. object more conveniently, use
     the `is_*()' methods below.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.linkname
     Name of the target file name, which is only present in *note
     TarInfo: d46. objects of type `LNKTYPE' and `SYMTYPE'.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.uid
     User ID of the user who originally stored this member.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.gid
     Group ID of the user who originally stored this member.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.uname
     User name.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.gname
     Group name.

 -- Attribute: TarInfo.pax_headers
     A dictionary containing key-value pairs of an associated pax
     extended header.

     New in version 2.6.

  A *note TarInfo: d46. object also provides some convenient query
methods:

 -- Method: TarInfo.isfile ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if the `Tarinfo' object is a regular file.

 -- Method: TarInfo.isreg ()
     Same as *note isfile: d64.

 -- Method: TarInfo.isdir ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a directory.

 -- Method: TarInfo.issym ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a symbolic link.

 -- Method: TarInfo.islnk ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a hard link.

 -- Method: TarInfo.ischr ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a character device.

 -- Method: TarInfo.isblk ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a block device.

 -- Method: TarInfo.isfifo ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is a FIFO.

 -- Method: TarInfo.isdev ()
     Return *note True: 18a. if it is one of character device, block
     device or FIFO.


