5.13.5 `xdrlib' -- Encode and decode XDR data
---------------------------------------------

The *note xdrlib: 78f. module supports the External Data Representation
Standard as described in RFC 1014
(http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1014.html), written by Sun Microsystems,
Inc. June 1987.  It supports most of the data types described in the
RFC.

  The *note xdrlib: 78f. module defines two classes, one for packing
variables into XDR representation, and another for unpacking from XDR
representation.  There are also two exception classes.

 -- Class: xdrlib.Packer
     *note Packer: dd9. is the class for packing data into XDR
     representation. The *note Packer: dd9. class is instantiated with
     no arguments.

 -- Class: xdrlib.Unpacker (data)
     `Unpacker' is the complementary class which unpacks XDR data
     values from a string buffer.  The input buffer is given as _data_.

RFC 1014 (http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1014.html) - XDR: External Data Representation Standard
     This RFC defined the encoding of data which was XDR at the time
     this module was originally written.  It has apparently been
     obsoleted by RFC 1832 (http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1832.html).

RFC 1832 (http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1832.html) - XDR: External Data Representation Standard
     Newer RFC that provides a revised definition of XDR.

