5.13.5.3 Exceptions
...................

Exceptions in this module are coded as class instances:

 -- Exception: xdrlib.Error
     The base exception class.  *note Error: df0. has a single public
     data member `msg' containing the description of the error.

 -- Exception: xdrlib.ConversionError
     Class derived from *note Error: df0.  Contains no additional
     instance variables.

  Here is an example of how you would catch one of these exceptions:

    import xdrlib
    p = xdrlib.Packer()
    try:
        p.pack_double(8.01)
    except xdrlib.ConversionError, instance:
        print 'packing the double failed:', instance.msg



