5.15.6.1 Logging tutorial
.........................

The key benefit of having the logging API provided by a standard
library module is that all Python modules can participate in logging,
so your application log can include messages from third-party modules.

  It is, of course, possible to log messages with different verbosity
levels or to different destinations.  Support for writing log messages
to files, HTTP GET/POST locations, email via SMTP, generic sockets, or
OS-specific logging mechanisms are all supported by the standard
module.  You can also create your own log destination class if you have
special requirements not met by any of the built-in classes.

