5.15.6.21 StreamHandler
.......................

The *note StreamHandler: fd9. class, located in the core *note logging:
b6. package, sends logging output to streams such as _sys.stdout_,
_sys.stderr_ or any file-like object (or, more precisely, any object
which supports `write()' and `flush()' methods).

 -- Class: logging.StreamHandler ([strm])
     Returns a new instance of the *note StreamHandler: fd9. class. If
     _strm_ is specified, the instance will use it for logging output;
     otherwise, _sys.stderr_ will be used.

      -- Method: emit (record)
          If a formatter is specified, it is used to format the record.
          The record is then written to the stream with a trailing
          newline. If exception information is present, it is formatted
          using *note traceback print_exception: 1029. and appended to
          the stream.

      -- Method: flush ()
          Flushes the stream by calling its *note flush: 102a. method.
          Note that the `close()' method is inherited from `Handler'
          and so does no output, so an explicit *note flush: 102a. call
          may be needed at times.


