5.16.2.9 Using locks, conditions, and semaphores in the `with' statement
........................................................................

All of the objects provided by this module that have `acquire()' and
`release()' methods can be used as context managers for a *note with:
17.  statement.  The `acquire()' method will be called when the block
is entered, and `release()' will be called when the block is exited.

  Currently, *note Lock: 12b4, *note RLock: 12b5, *note Condition: 12cf,
*note Semaphore: 12d7, and *note BoundedSemaphore: 12b6. objects may be
used as *note with: 17. statement context managers.  For example:

    import threading

    some_rlock = threading.RLock()

    with some_rlock:
        print "some_rlock is locked while this executes"



