5.17.4.1 Example
................

Here is a minimal example program. It uses the *note alarm: 144b.
function to limit the time spent waiting to open a file; this is useful
if the file is for a serial device that may not be turned on, which
would normally cause the *note os open: 3ec. to hang indefinitely.  The
solution is to set a 5-second alarm before opening the file; if the
operation takes too long, the alarm signal will be sent, and the
handler raises an exception.

    import signal, os

    def handler(signum, frame):
        print 'Signal handler called with signal', signum
        raise IOError("Couldn't open device!")

    # Set the signal handler and a 5-second alarm
    signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, handler)
    signal.alarm(5)

    # This open() may hang indefinitely
    fd = os.open('/dev/ttyS0', os.O_RDWR)

    signal.alarm(0)          # Disable the alarm



