5.20.5 `urllib' -- Open arbitrary resources by URL
--------------------------------------------------

     Note: The *note urllib: 279. module has been split into parts and
     renamed in Python 3.0 to `urllib.request', `urllib.parse', and
     `urllib.error'. The *note 2to3: 945. tool will automatically adapt
     imports when converting your sources to 3.0.  Also note that the
     *note urllib urlopen: e8. function has been removed in Python 3.0
     in favor of *note urllib2 urlopen: e9.

This module provides a high-level interface for fetching data across
the World Wide Web.  In particular, the *note urlopen: e8. function is
similar to the built-in function *note open: 1b, but accepts Universal
Resource Locators (URLs) instead of filenames.  Some restrictions apply
-- it can only open URLs for reading, and no seek operations are
available.

* Menu:

* High-level interface::
