7.7.5.10 CObjects
.................

Refer to *note Providing a C API for an Extension Module: 262e. for
more information on using these objects.

 -- type: PyCObject
     This subtype of *note PyObject: 17e. represents an opaque value,
     useful for C extension modules who need to pass an opaque value
     (as a `void*' pointer) through Python code to other C code.  It is
     often used to make a C function pointer defined in one module
     available to other modules, so the regular import mechanism can be
     used to access C APIs defined in dynamically loaded modules.

 -- Function: int PyCObject_Check (PyObject *p)
     Return true if its argument is a *note PyCObject: 2962.

 -- Function: PyObject* PyCObject_FromVoidPtr (void* cobj, void
          (*destr)(void *))
     Return value: New reference.

     Create a *note PyCObject: 2962. from the `void *' _cobj_.  The
     _destr_ function will be called when the object is reclaimed,
     unless it is _NULL_.

 -- Function: PyObject* PyCObject_FromVoidPtrAndDesc (void* cobj, void*
          desc, void (*destr)(void *, void *))
     Return value: New reference.

     Create a *note PyCObject: 2962. from the `void *' _cobj_.  The
     _destr_ function will be called when the object is reclaimed. The
     _desc_ argument can be used to pass extra callback data for the
     destructor function.

 -- Function: void* PyCObject_AsVoidPtr (PyObject* self)
     Return the object `void *' that the *note PyCObject: 2962. _self_
     was created with.

 -- Function: void* PyCObject_GetDesc (PyObject* self)
     Return the description `void *' that the *note PyCObject: 2962.
     _self_ was created with.

 -- Function: int PyCObject_SetVoidPtr (PyObject* self, void* cobj)
     Set the void pointer inside _self_ to _cobj_. The *note PyCObject:
     2962. must not have an associated destructor. Return true on
     success, false on failure.


