7.10.5 Mapping Object Structures
--------------------------------

 -- type: PyMappingMethods
     This structure holds pointers to the functions which an object
     uses to implement the mapping protocol.  It has three members:

 -- member: lenfunc PyMappingMethods.mp_length
     This function is used by *note PyMapping_Length: 2796. and *note
     PyObject_Size: 2748, and has the same signature.  This slot may be
     set to _NULL_ if the object has no defined length.

 -- member: binaryfunc PyMappingMethods.mp_subscript
     This function is used by *note PyObject_GetItem: 2685. and has the
     same signature.  This slot must be filled for the *note
     PyMapping_Check: 2794.  function to return `1', it can be _NULL_
     otherwise.

 -- member: objobjargproc PyMappingMethods.mp_ass_subscript
     This function is used by *note PyObject_SetItem: 2683. and has the
     same signature.  If this slot is _NULL_, the object does not
     support item assignment.


