7.10.6 Sequence Object Structures
---------------------------------

 -- type: PySequenceMethods
     This structure holds pointers to the functions which an object
     uses to implement the sequence protocol.

 -- member: lenfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_length
     This function is used by *note PySequence_Size: 277d. and *note
     PyObject_Size: 2748, and has the same signature.

 -- member: binaryfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_concat
     This function is used by *note PySequence_Concat: 277f. and has
     the same signature.  It is also used by the `+' operator, after
     trying the numeric addition via the `tp_as_number.nb_add' slot.

 -- member: ssizeargfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_repeat
     This function is used by *note PySequence_Repeat: 2780. and has
     the same signature.  It is also used by the `*' operator, after
     trying numeric multiplication via the `tp_as_number.nb_mul' slot.

 -- member: ssizeargfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_item
     This function is used by *note PySequence_GetItem: 2686. and has
     the same signature.  This slot must be filled for the *note
     PySequence_Check: 277c.  function to return `1', it can be _NULL_
     otherwise.

     Negative indexes are handled as follows: if the `sq_length' slot is
     filled, it is called and the sequence length is used to compute a
     positive index which is passed to `sq_item'.  If `sq_length' is
     _NULL_, the index is passed as is to the function.

 -- member: ssizeobjargproc PySequenceMethods.sq_ass_item
     This function is used by *note PySequence_SetItem: 2682. and has
     the same signature.  This slot may be left to _NULL_ if the object
     does not support item assignment.

 -- member: objobjproc PySequenceMethods.sq_contains
     This function may be used by *note PySequence_Contains: 2788. and
     has the same signature.  This slot may be left to _NULL_, in this
     case *note PySequence_Contains: 2788. simply traverses the
     sequence until it finds a match.

 -- member: binaryfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_inplace_concat
     This function is used by *note PySequence_InPlaceConcat: 2781. and
     has the same signature.  It should modify its first operand, and
     return it.

 -- member: ssizeargfunc PySequenceMethods.sq_inplace_repeat
     This function is used by *note PySequence_InPlaceRepeat: 2782. and
     has the same signature.  It should modify its first operand, and
     return it.


